    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Students at "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "Purdue University",
            "zh": "普渡大学"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " have built a robot that can solve a Rubik’s Cube faster than anyone ever imagined. They call it “Purdubik’s Cube”. The robot solves a cube in just 0.103 seconds. That’s faster than the time it takes to blink your eyes!"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The Rubik’s Cube was invented in 1974 by Erno Rubik and quickly became popular worldwide. At first, people just wanted to solve the puzzle. But soon, a new group of enthusiasts emerged—“speedcubers”, who aim to solve the cube as quickly as possible. The fastest human can solve a cube in about 3.05 seconds. Amazing, right? But robots can do it even quicker. In 2020, MIT students built a robot that solved a cube in 0.380 seconds. This left a deep impression on Matthew Patrohay, who was in high school at the time. “I thought, ‘That’s a really cool project. I’d love to try and beat it someday,’” said Mr. Patrohay."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Now, Mr. Patrohay and three other Purdue students have built a robot that beat that record. Their robot uses cameras and computer vision to detect the colours of each square. Special computer programs tell the robot how to move, and its arms turn the cube at "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "incredible",
            "ref": "v-incredible"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " speed. The students even made a stronger cube so it wouldn’t fall apart. Bluetooth technology lets users "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "scramble",
            "ref": "v-scramble"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " the cube "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "remotely",
            "ref": "v-remotely"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". Once scrambled, the robot solves it almost instantly. Its movements are so fast that “before you even realise it’s moving, we’ve solved it,” says Mr. Patrohay."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "i1",
        "type": "imageRef",
        "image": "img1"
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Last year, the students won a school design contest with Purdubik’s Cube. After that, they kept improving it, and their efforts paid off. Now, it proudly holds the Guinness World Record for the fastest robot to solve a Rubik’s Cube. One of the students’ professors says he’s not surprised. “Take brilliant students, give them the tools and opportunities, and they’ll blow your mind,” he said."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
